f2fs: put kobjects when kobject_init_and_add() fails in f2fs_init_sysfs()

kobject_init_and_add() initialises the kobject before it can fail, so the
caller must kobject_put() it on failure as well; otherwise the kobject name
allocated by kobject_set_name_vargs() leaks. Since the unwind was split, a
failure to add "features" skips kobject_put(&f2fs_feat) and a failure to add
"tuning" skips kobject_put(&f2fs_tune). kmemleak reports the names
("features", "tuning") after fault injection makes module loading fail.

Put each kobject from its own failure path; f2fs_tune is still only put
once it has been initialised.

Fixes: b635f2ecdb5a ("f2fs: fix uninitialized kobject put in f2fs_init_sysfs()")
---
--- a/fs/f2fs/sysfs.c	2026-10-20 16:38:32.582231828 +0000
+++ b/fs/f2fs/sysfs.c	2026-10-20 16:38:55.203759345 +0000
@@ -1936,15 +1936,16 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* kobject_init_and_add() needs kobject_put() on failure, too. */
 	ret = kobject_init_and_add(&f2fs_feat, &f2fs_feat_ktype,
 				   NULL, "features");
 	if (ret)
-		goto unregister_kset;
+		goto put_feat;
 
 	ret = kobject_init_and_add(&f2fs_tune, &f2fs_tune_ktype,
 				   NULL, "tuning");
 	if (ret)
-		goto put_feat;
+		goto put_tune;
 
 	f2fs_proc_root = proc_mkdir("fs/f2fs", NULL);
 	if (!f2fs_proc_root) {
@@ -1958,7 +1959,6 @@
 	kobject_put(&f2fs_tune);
 put_feat:
 	kobject_put(&f2fs_feat);
-unregister_kset:
 	kset_unregister(&f2fs_kset);
 	return ret;
 }
